# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build an interactive application that implements and compares:

1. Stop-and-Wait ARQ.
2. Go-Back-N ARQ.
3. Selective Repeat ARQ.
4. AURA-BOLT Adaptive ARQ, which dynamically selects appropriate configurations based on observed network conditions.

The application should investigate whether a burst-aware, recovery-cost-based adaptive controller can improve useful throughput and transfer efficiency while respecting latency and receiver-buffer constraints.

The system must support:

- Sender and receiver simulation.
- Real file transfer between separate processes.
- Packet loss and acknowledgement loss.
- Network delay and jitter.
- Out-of-order packet delivery.
- Retransmission timeouts.
- Sliding-window visualization.
- Burst-loss detection.
- Adaptive window-size selection.
- Adaptive retransmission-timeout estimation.
- Performance measurement.
- Comparative experiments.
- File-integrity verification.

