# 11. PREDICT, APPLY, VERIFY LOOP

Implement the following closed-loop process:

STEP 1 — OBSERVE

Collect current network and protocol measurements.

STEP 2 — PREDICT

Evaluate feasible candidate configurations using the recovery-cost model.

STEP 3 — SELECT

Choose a configuration according to the defined objective and constraints.

STEP 4 — APPLY

Apply the configuration safely at the appropriate protocol boundary.

STEP 5 — MEASURE

Collect the actual post-change performance.

STEP 6 — VERIFY

Compare predicted and measured results.

STEP 7 — UPDATE

Record prediction error and update model estimates where appropriate.

STEP 8 — FALLBACK

If measurements are unreliable or performance violates configured constraints, revert to a safe configuration.

Store a complete audit trail.

